      "Language": "dan",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A woman who had formerly had adequately treated breast cancer presented with symptoms of pain in the right shin. An X-ray of the punctum maximum for the pain showed a bone lesion. Biopsy revealed that it came from an adenocarcinoma of the lung, contrary to the first diagnosis of breast cancer meta-stasis. The lung lesion had been seen on a subsequent computed tomography. There were no presenting symptoms relating to lung cancer. This case is interesting as adenocarcinoma metastasis to bone rarely occurs in the tibia and below the knee."},
